cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  SyndrumNET: a Python implementation of network-based
  prediction of synergistic drug combinations
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this
  repository and the Iida et al. (2024) paper that
  describes the method it implements.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aslanzade
    given-names: Nihad
    alias: nihadaslanzade-02
repository-code: https://github.com/nihadaslanzade-02/SyndrumNET
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - drug-combinations
  - drug-synergy
  - network-propagation
  - network-medicine
  - systems-biology
  - bioinformatics
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of SyndrumNET, a network-based
  trans-omics method for predicting synergistic drug
  combinations. Integrates molecular-interaction resources
  into a single human interactome, builds gene modules for
  diseases and drugs from expression signatures, propagates
  signal with PRINCE, and scores drug pairs on network
  topology, disease proximity and transcriptional reversal.
  The scoring layer is complete and tested; parts of the
  data layer are placeholders, documented in
  docs/PLACEHOLDERS.md.
